  "texts": {
    "preamble": "T Venkateswara Raju vs State Of Andhra Pradesh on 21 January, 2020 Author: T. Rajani Bench: T. Rajani Smt Justice T. Rajani Criminal Petition No.222 Of 2020 Order:",
    "facts": "This petition is filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C., seeking to quash the proceedings against the petitioner, who is accused, in Crime No.131 of 2019 on the file of the Station House Officer, Gudlur Police Station, Prakasam District, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 273, 328, 420 IPC and Sections 59 & 63 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (FSS Act). 2.",
    "arguments": "3. The counsel for the petitioner submits that in similar circumstances, this Court by virtue of the order dated 13.9.2019 passed in Crl.P.No.5254 of 2019 [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the accused therein by holding that tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(1)(j) of the FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of the FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. The counsel for the petitioner submits that in similar circumstances, this Court by virtue of the order dated 13.9.2019 passed in Crl.P.No.5254 of 2019 [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the accused therein by holding that tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(1)(j) of the FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of the FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
